      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13177",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_n = (-1)^n \\,n, \\qquad n \\in \\mathbb N = \\{1,2,3,4,\\ldots\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =(-1)^{1}(1)=-1 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =(-1)^{2}(2)=2 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =(-1)^{3}(3)=-3 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =(-1)^{4}(4)=4 \\\\  & \u22ee\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\nA = \\{ -1, 2, -3, 4,  \\ldots \\}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038029/example-13177.json",
