      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13142",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The condition after the \"$:$\" symbol, \n\n$$\nn \\in \\mathbb Z,\\, -2\\leq n\\leq 2\n$$\n\nstates that $n$ can be any integer that satisfies the inequality $-2\\leq n\\leq 2.$ \n\nTherefore, the elements of $A$ are all the terms of the sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_n = 4^n, \\qquad n \\in \\{0, \\pm 1, \\pm 2\\}.\n$$\n\nLet's write down all the terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{-2} & ={4}^{-2}=\\frac{1}{16} \\\\ {a}_{-1} & ={4}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {a}_{0} & ={4}^{0}=1 \\\\ {a}_{1} & ={4}^{1}=4 \\\\ {a}_{2} & ={4}^{2}=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{\\dfrac{1}{16},\\,\\dfrac{1}{4},\\,1,\\,4,\\,16 \\right\\}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038029/example-13142.json",
          "file_sha256": "f77b93f7c76c822d258f9b5f9dedb1877179ca13ada4682d4d9d54a44fbaf917"
        }
