      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-13285",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The elements of $A$ are all the terms of the *recursive* sequence $a_n,$ given by\n\n$$\na_{n+1} =2a_{n} - 1, \\quad a_1 =2,\\qquad n \\in \\mathbb N.\n$$\n\nLet's write down the first few terms of our sequence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1} & =2 \\\\ {a}_{2} & =2{a}_{1}-1 \\\\  & =2(2)-1 \\\\  & =3 \\\\ {a}_{3} & =2{a}_{2}-1 \\\\  & =2(3)-1 \\\\  & =5 \\\\ {a}_{4} & =2{a}_{3}-1 \\\\  & =2(5)-1 \\\\  & =9 \\\\ {a}_{5} & =2{a}_{4}-1 \\\\  & =2(9)-1 \\\\  & =17 \\\\  & \u22ee\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\nA = \\left\\{2,3,5,9,17,\\ldots \\right\\}.\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14038029/example-13285.json",
